08003C20 TerrainOverlay_Update stale body (sprite read at 08003D00)

Armor_InitFromScript queues its body with the overlay. Armor_Destroy
unregisters that body with SceneBody_Unregister, leaving the overlay entry
live when the reward reuses the actor storage. In the power-on movie in
scene 2803, r4 at the original sprite read still names 0200E3E0 and r1
becomes 800010E0 at mGBA frame 70513. The ROM continues through the read.
The corresponding wasm access traps outside linear memory at port frame
69282. Validate the body against the live registry before dereferencing it.

The explicit form differed. The guarded copy matched the full 1660-byte
translation unit at 08003B44 with the stock compiler.

--- a/src/scene/terrain/terrain_overlay.c
+++ b/src/scene/terrain/terrain_overlay.c
@@ -125,6 +125,15 @@
         s32 quadrant, yFixed, y, x, z;
         if (!entry->used)
             continue;
+#ifdef UBFIX
+        /* SceneBody_Unregister can leave the overlay holding a recycled body. */
+        if (SceneBody_GetById(entry->id) != actor) {
+            entry->used = 0;
+            entry->id = 0;
+            entry->actor = 0;
+            continue;
+        }
+#endif
         if (actor->keyframeDisplay && (actor->keyframeDisplay->flags & 1))
             continue;
         {
